1
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:34,970
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,060
[Episode 1]

3
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:41,509
In 1941,

4
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,009
the Japanese Army began preparations

5
00:01:44,009 --> 00:01:46,410
for biological warfare in northern China.

6
00:01:46,590 --> 00:01:48,009
They established

7
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:49,490
Unit 1644 in Nanjing

8
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,160
and secretly set up

9
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:53,770
a biological research institute
in Shanghai,

10
00:01:54,009 --> 00:01:56,280
code-naming the operation

11
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,729
Project Slumber.

12
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,940
Diana, an underground
Communist Party member,

13
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:02,790
was ordered

14
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,940
to obtain the research findings

15
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,750
and operational plans

16
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,639
before Project Slumber

17
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,660
could be fully implemented.

18
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:17,900
[Diana, underground CPC member]

19
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:35,140
[Lu Xiaoguang, underground CPC member]

20
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:44,590
[Wake up Broken Bridge]

21
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:04,100
[Li Musheng, underground CPC member]

22
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:13,360
Okay, thank you.

23
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:14,870
Sir.

24
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:16,870
Welcome.

25
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:18,670
Sir, I'd like to develop a photo.

26
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:19,400
Alright.

27
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:23,150
Is that camera American-made?

28
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,060
It's German-made.

29
00:03:26,950 --> 00:03:28,000
I heard they have

30
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:29,310
color film now.

31
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:31,030
Yes.

32
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,400
However,

33
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,090
I still prefer black and white.

34
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,280
Black is black,

35
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:37,450
and white is white.

36
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,310
[Chen Kailai, photographer]

37
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:43,440
Develop a four-inch one.

38
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,000
Okay.

39
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,079
When you pick up the photo,

40
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:49,880
remember to bring this receipt.

41
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,079
Okay.

42
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,430
Three yuan.

43
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:54,950
Thank you.

44
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,000
Take care.

45
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,340
Come again.

46
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:09,360
Why do you need
a magnifying glass to develop photos?

47
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,760
I'm getting presbyopic.

48
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:20,070
Go to Shanghai,

49
00:05:20,810 --> 00:05:24,340
open Fulai Photo Studio,

50
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:29,860
and wait for Su Causeway.

51
00:06:04,310 --> 00:06:05,160
Thank you.

52
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:06,160
Take care.

53
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:08,190
Come again.

54
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,480
Kailai.

55
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:13,770
What's the date today?

56
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,070
The 23rd.

57
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:18,670
So that means this month,

58
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,340
you've worked for 23 days, right?

59
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,490
I'll pay you a full month's salary.

60
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:27,630
Take it.

61
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:28,950
Go now.

62
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,090
What do you mean?

63
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,850
This Chunguang Photo Studio—

64
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:33,850
I want to close it.

65
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:39,040
Are you sick?

66
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:40,680
Don't jinx me.

67
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:41,920
Take it.

68
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,000
I want to go to Shanghai

69
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,159
and open a new photo studio.

70
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:49,950
Li Musheng,

71
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:52,070
are you making fun of me?

72
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:56,190
I'm being serious.

73
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,880
Then take me with you.

74
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:01,070
Take you?

75
00:07:01,510 --> 00:07:02,240
I can't.

76
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,370
Thank you, officer.

77
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,630
Over there! Shoot!

78
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:45,430
[Suzuki, Japanese official]

79
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:17,100
Go to Zhongmei Cafe Dancing Hall.

80
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,320
Mr. Suzuki...

81
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:18,960
It's okay.

82
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:31,120
I will finish what I promised.

83
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,049
I'll leave after taking the photo
for old Mr. Wei.

84
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:39,080
What's the repertoire
for tonight's performance?

85
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,409
"Empty Fort Strategy."

86
00:08:43,909 --> 00:08:44,630
Li Musheng,

87
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,660
you are playing
the Empty Fort Strategy with me.

88
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,670
Miss Meizhen,

89
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,320
may I have this dance?

90
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:26,240
[Jinbao, dancing girl]

91
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:24,120
Sorry, Mr. Wu.

92
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,310
I've already agreed to dance with someone.

93
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:27,440
I'm waiting for him.

94
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,740
I saw you sitting here
as soon as I came in.

95
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,280
I'm afraid he won't come today.

96
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,600
He will.

97
00:10:04,570 --> 00:10:08,500
[Tao Dachun,
captain of the NBIS Hurricane Team]

98
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:09,840
Let me go!

99
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:12,080
Let me go! What are you doing?

100
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,510
What are you doing?

101
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,030
Let go!

102
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:14,030
Mr. Suzuki,

103
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,600
since you have something to do today,

104
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,000
let's dance another day.

105
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,080
Meizhen,

106
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,480
I came here specially for you.

107
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:25,310
People who don't know the situation

108
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:26,970
would think dancing is a crime

109
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:29,830
and I could be arrested
and imprisoned at any time.

110
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,270
Forgive me.

111
00:11:37,910 --> 00:11:39,000
It's so lame.

112
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:40,670
With them staring at me like this,

113
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:42,150
I can't even enjoy myself.

114
00:11:42,390 --> 00:11:43,120
Another day.

115
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:46,270
Tonight,

116
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:49,550
I want to dance until I die.

117
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:51,840
Mr. Suzuki,

118
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,450
you don't want to dance.

119
00:11:58,670 --> 00:12:00,000
Then I'll do as you wish.

120
00:12:10,710 --> 00:12:13,030
Go drive the car
to the door and wait for me.

121
00:12:13,030 --> 00:12:15,890
I'll smoke a cigarette
and leave here immediately.

122
00:12:16,270 --> 00:12:16,840
Yes.

123
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:30,850
It's like eloping.

124
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:33,810
Where are we going?

125
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,900
I'm a little tired.

126
00:12:35,870 --> 00:12:37,200
Then I'll take you home.

127
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:17,000
We are here.

128
00:13:17,610 --> 00:13:18,140
Let's go.

129
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:21,600
Here.

130
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:23,800
Let's go.

131
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:24,730
Okay.

132
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,030
Who is it?

133
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,300
It's an emergency.

134
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:22,480
Major, we are exposed!

135
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,870
Charge in and catch him!

136
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:24,510
Yes!

137
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:07,980
Don't let him escape!

138
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,660
Mr. Broken Bridge.

139
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,490
Do you have any companions?

140
00:17:01,070 --> 00:17:12,579
♪ I was watching the scenery
from the city tower ♪

141
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:24,440
♪ When I heard the chaos
outside the city ♪

142
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,590
♪ Banners fluttering in the wind ♪

143
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:30,510
Shut up!

144
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:46,680
♪ It turns out they're the troops ♪

145
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:54,890
♪ Sima brought here ♪

146
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,590
Singing opera at a time like this?

147
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:13,160
You're scared to death, aren't you?

148
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:45,410
Did he have any accomplices?

149
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:46,590
I don't know.

150
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:49,770
I don't know.
I'm just here delivering the film.

151
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:51,760
But there's another assistant

152
00:18:52,110 --> 00:18:53,510
at the photo studio.

153
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,480
Go check!

154
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:57,270
Yes!

155
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,810
Where is Suzuki?

156
00:19:45,010 --> 00:19:45,860
He's asleep.

157
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:54,000
Go now.

158
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:03,960
♪ I was watching... ♪

159
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:12,710
♪ I was watching the scenery
from the city tower ♪

160
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:19,720
♪ When I heard the chaos
outside the city ♪

161
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:23,720
♪ Banners fluttering in the wind ♪

162
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:28,590
♪ I was watching the scenery ♪

163
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:36,240
♪ From the city tower ♪

164
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:40,680
♪ When I heard the chaos
outside the city ♪

165
00:21:41,790 --> 00:21:43,960
♪ They're the troops ♪

166
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:48,590
♪ Sima brought here ♪

167
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,510
Go...

168
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:51,920
find...

169
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,240
them.

170
00:24:12,810 --> 00:24:14,200
Yes, I see.

171
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:17,000
I will definitely find Suzuki.

172
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:28,160
Why did Suzuki suddenly lose contact?

173
00:24:28,750 --> 00:24:31,430
Mr. Suzuki might have gone on a date.

174
00:24:33,270 --> 00:24:34,000
A date?

175
00:24:37,510 --> 00:24:38,570
Sir, your wontons.

176
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:51,390
What terrible weather it is.

177
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:52,780
I'm a ballroom queen.

178
00:24:53,060 --> 00:24:55,220
What if my ankles get frostbitten?

179
00:24:56,190 --> 00:24:57,160
Why are you here?

180
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,200
Today is my birthday.

181
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:03,120
Why am I so unlucky

182
00:25:03,330 --> 00:25:04,790
as to live right above you?

183
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:07,510
You know him so well.

184
00:25:07,910 --> 00:25:10,170
How did you not realize he's a Communist?

185
00:25:13,870 --> 00:25:15,110
Are you one too?

186
00:25:15,130 --> 00:25:16,080
Nonsense!

187
00:25:18,310 --> 00:25:19,310
I haven't eaten yet.

188
00:25:19,310 --> 00:25:20,640
Where are your manners?

189
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,400
Sir, another bowl here.

190
00:25:22,420 --> 00:25:23,140
No need!

191
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,500
Take your time.

192
00:25:27,260 --> 00:25:28,300
Don't go.

193
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:29,450
Where are you going?

194
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:39,530
A soldier should die on the battlefield.

195
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:42,160
Why did you die in a woman's bed?

196
00:25:42,790 --> 00:25:43,480
Major.

197
00:25:44,750 --> 00:25:46,510
No briefcase was found.

198
00:25:47,070 --> 00:25:47,920
When he left,

199
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,830
he had the briefcase with him.

200
00:25:51,220 --> 00:25:52,480
Go over there quickly.

201
00:25:55,830 --> 00:25:58,000
The dancer on the 2nd floor
is not Meizhen.

202
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,400
She told me her name is...

203
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,550
Wang... Wang Xiaoni.

204
00:26:01,790 --> 00:26:04,570
The assistant at the photo studio
is called Chen Kailai.

205
00:26:04,570 --> 00:26:05,770
Chen Kailai!

206
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:07,960
Where are they?

207
00:26:09,590 --> 00:26:10,350
I don't know.

208
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:12,350
I... I don't know.

209
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,060
Don't move.

210
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:20,050
You are a Communist.

211
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:21,740
Give me your money.

212
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:26,740
Is this fun for you?

213
00:26:27,650 --> 00:26:29,780
It seems you have a guilty conscience.

214
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:31,720
Can you stop following me?

215
00:26:31,740 --> 00:26:32,900
Who's following you?

216
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:34,100
I'm on this train too.

217
00:26:36,670 --> 00:26:38,410
Something happened to the photo studio,
and now you're in a hurry to run away.

218
00:26:38,410 --> 00:26:40,070
You must have a guilty conscience.

219
00:26:40,070 --> 00:26:42,000
Can I explain myself if I don't run?

220
00:26:42,160 --> 00:26:43,380
You're the one with a guilty conscience.

221
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:44,160
It has nothing to do with you.

222
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,000
Why are you also running away?

223
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,110
I can't explain myself either.

224
00:26:46,110 --> 00:26:47,270
Why do you need to explain yourself?

225
00:26:47,270 --> 00:26:48,350
You're not from the photo studio.

226
00:26:48,350 --> 00:26:49,680
Didn't you drag me into this?

227
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:50,790
Nonsense.

228
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:52,730
Who dragged you into this?

229
00:26:53,130 --> 00:26:54,730
Perfect. We can go together.

230
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:00,920
Be careful. Be careful.

231
00:27:03,920 --> 00:27:04,520
Excuse me.

232
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:05,790
We finally got on.

233
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:08,330
You really think you're a big shot?

234
00:27:08,510 --> 00:27:11,240
Who cares about investigating
a nobody like you?

235
00:27:13,790 --> 00:27:15,920
Move forward. Don't just stand there.

236
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:36,400
Sorry, Major!

237
00:27:38,310 --> 00:27:40,720
I'm not the one you should be sorry to.

238
00:28:21,130 --> 00:28:22,720
It's Christmas again.

239
00:28:25,410 --> 00:28:28,060
I didn't expect Hangzhou to get snow.

240
00:28:28,090 --> 00:28:29,610
It looks like Nara.

241
00:28:55,790 --> 00:28:57,390
What are you thinking about?

242
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:03,440
Are we all at the mercy of fate?

243
00:29:04,920 --> 00:29:07,030
Yesterday I was filming
a private performance.

244
00:29:07,030 --> 00:29:08,360
And today I'm on a train.

245
00:29:09,110 --> 00:29:10,310
It feels like a dream.

246
00:29:11,350 --> 00:29:12,480
We've already left.

247
00:29:13,030 --> 00:29:14,960
What's the use of thinking so much?

248
00:29:19,590 --> 00:29:21,850
How much money did your master leave you?

249
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:24,210
What money could he have left?

250
00:29:24,750 --> 00:29:26,550
He didn't even give me my salary.

251
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:28,920
Then where did you get the money
for the ticket?

252
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:31,720
I got paid for the performance filming
yesterday.

253
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:36,440
At least he left you a camera.

254
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:38,810
It should be worth something.

255
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:42,840
Why are you always talking about money?

256
00:29:43,110 --> 00:29:45,640
How can we survive in Shanghai
without money?

257
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:47,790
You are you, and I am me.

258
00:29:48,110 --> 00:29:49,200
There is no "we."

259
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,590
Where are you going?

260
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:55,750
I want to be alone.

261
00:29:56,510 --> 00:29:57,880
Why are you always avoiding me?

262
00:29:57,880 --> 00:29:58,860
You're not normal.

263
00:29:58,860 --> 00:30:00,110
You're the one who's not normal.

264
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:01,960
You're going to Shanghai
without any luggage.

265
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:02,820
Is that normal?

266
00:30:05,620 --> 00:30:07,520
That's why I'm dragging you along.

267
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:08,080
You...

268
00:30:08,110 --> 00:30:09,350
Ticket inspection.

269
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:11,040
Have your tickets ready.

270
00:30:15,230 --> 00:30:17,310
Look at you, acting so guilty.

271
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:19,240
I'm afraid you'll drag me down.

272
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:21,510
Come on.

273
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:22,880
Let me take you somewhere.

274
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:23,680
I'm not going.

275
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,160
You're not going?

276
00:30:26,510 --> 00:30:27,840
Well, think carefully.

277
00:30:28,310 --> 00:30:29,590
If I make a scene,

278
00:30:29,790 --> 00:30:31,240
maybe someone

279
00:30:31,260 --> 00:30:32,950
will really notice you later.

280
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:34,350
Let's go.

281
00:30:35,460 --> 00:30:36,110
Let's go.

282
00:30:41,550 --> 00:30:42,270
Come here.

283
00:30:47,510 --> 00:30:49,040
No one checks tickets here.

284
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,330
Just buy something.

285
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:53,160
Do you know why I don't have luggage?

286
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,400
Money is enough.

287
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,460
If you have money,
why did you eat my wontons?

288
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,480
Aren't I paying you back now?

289
00:31:03,620 --> 00:31:05,150
Waiter, we'd like to order.

290
00:31:11,010 --> 00:31:11,790
Give him a menu too.

291
00:31:11,790 --> 00:31:12,350
Okay.

292
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:22,770
This is enough for 10 bowls of wontons.

293
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:27,160
I want this.

294
00:31:27,920 --> 00:31:28,510
This.

295
00:31:29,270 --> 00:31:29,880
This.

296
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:30,960
And this.

297
00:31:31,510 --> 00:31:32,710
Two portions of each.

298
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:33,350
Okay.

299
00:31:34,070 --> 00:31:35,240
Two glasses of water.

300
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:35,920
That's all.

301
00:31:36,350 --> 00:31:37,000
Okay.

302
00:32:05,310 --> 00:32:07,110
You don't appreciate my kindness?

303
00:32:07,110 --> 00:32:08,440
I don't live off women.

304
00:32:08,850 --> 00:32:10,450
This isn't living off women.

305
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:13,720
I'm inviting you to my birthday party.

306
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:15,830
You're not going to do me the honor?

307
00:32:15,830 --> 00:32:16,550
Fine.

308
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:26,400
Where are you going?

309
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,120
Restroom.

310
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:44,440
Thank you.

311
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:45,850
Enjoy your meal.

312
00:33:00,710 --> 00:33:02,440
The weather is nice today.

313
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:04,590
I took a car to the riverside.

314
00:33:05,830 --> 00:33:07,510
The river was sparkling.

315
00:33:08,110 --> 00:33:11,370
It was so quiet there
that I could almost hear my heartbeat.

316
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:14,590
The surrounding willow trees
were swaying gently in the wind.

317
00:33:14,590 --> 00:33:15,960
It's his lover.

318
00:33:26,620 --> 00:33:27,820
You've been in there for a long time.

319
00:33:27,820 --> 00:33:28,450
Sorry.

320
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:42,020
[Cui Enxi, bodyguard to the special commissioner
of the Nanjing National Government]

321
00:33:55,900 --> 00:33:56,580
Come here.

322
00:33:57,420 --> 00:34:00,080
It seems there really is a big shot
on this train.

323
00:34:11,130 --> 00:34:13,909
[Su Men, special commissioner
of the Nanjing National Government]

324
00:34:28,150 --> 00:34:29,480
What are you looking at?

325
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:31,030
The big shot.

326
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:35,940
What does a big shot have to do with us?

327
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:38,550
Even if it's the Jade Emperor,

328
00:34:38,550 --> 00:34:40,610
it's not as important as my birthday.

329
00:34:43,030 --> 00:34:43,960
Happy birthday.

330
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:47,920
Do you have a birthday present for me?

331
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:48,550
No.

332
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,590
I knew it.

333
00:34:53,250 --> 00:34:54,310
Take a picture of me

334
00:34:54,670 --> 00:34:56,000
as my birthday present.

335
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:57,590
That's easy.

336
00:35:07,100 --> 00:35:08,560
My left side looks better.

337
00:35:14,710 --> 00:35:15,710
Take another one.

338
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,050
My right side is not bad either.

339
00:35:33,630 --> 00:35:35,430
What are you taking pictures of?

340
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:37,190
None of your business.

341
00:35:37,190 --> 00:35:39,000
Can't we take pictures of a beauty?

342
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:39,860
Take them away.

343
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,400
Get up.

344
00:35:42,430 --> 00:35:44,480
-Where are you taking us?
-What are you doing?

345
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:45,230
What are you doing?

346
00:35:45,230 --> 00:35:45,760
Go!

347
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:46,440
Let me go!

348
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:51,320
Let me go!

349
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:51,920
Hurry!

350
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:53,760
Let me go!

351
00:35:53,790 --> 00:35:54,390
Hurry!

352
00:35:54,410 --> 00:35:55,470
Where are we going?

353
00:35:56,950 --> 00:35:57,590
The bag.

354
00:35:58,550 --> 00:35:59,760
Let go! Let go of it!

355
00:36:01,540 --> 00:36:02,140
Your arm.

356
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:09,670
Get in! Go!

357
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:10,280
Let me go!

358
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:10,680
Get in!

359
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:50,680
There's nothing.

360
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:52,540
He should just be a photographer.

361
00:37:00,570 --> 00:37:01,220
Come here.

362
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:11,200
Do you know me?

363
00:37:12,370 --> 00:37:13,300
I don't know you.

364
00:37:22,510 --> 00:37:24,510
Then why did you take a picture of me?

365
00:37:25,670 --> 00:37:27,030
I'm a photographer.

366
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,670
I took it on impulse.

367
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:30,800
Who told you that a photographer

368
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:32,660
can just take pictures of anyone?

369
00:37:33,550 --> 00:37:34,410
At that moment,

370
00:37:35,490 --> 00:37:38,090
I thought you looked like
a piece of porcelain.

371
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,190
Porcelain?

372
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:44,770
Very exquisite.

373
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,810
What are you going to Shanghai for?

374
00:37:53,810 --> 00:37:54,610
To try my luck.

375
00:37:55,150 --> 00:37:55,840
How?

376
00:37:57,280 --> 00:37:58,550
Besides taking pictures,

377
00:37:58,550 --> 00:37:59,950
there's nothing I can do.

378
00:38:04,760 --> 00:38:05,550
What is it?

379
00:38:07,770 --> 00:38:08,900
Works I shot before.

380
00:38:17,030 --> 00:38:18,760
Do you know anyone in Shanghai?

381
00:38:19,230 --> 00:38:19,960
No.

382
00:38:22,070 --> 00:38:22,960
You're lying.

383
00:38:26,510 --> 00:38:28,150
"Written in Shanghai."

384
00:38:30,290 --> 00:38:31,820
The letter in this notebook

385
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:34,780
was written to you
by someone from Shanghai.

386
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:36,710
That's a pen pal.

387
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:38,220
We've never even met.

388
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:40,940
That still counts
as knowing someone there.

389
00:38:41,710 --> 00:38:43,170
If you put it that way, yes.

390
00:38:46,030 --> 00:38:47,160
Don't try to fool me.

391
00:38:58,230 --> 00:38:59,230
What are you doing?

392
00:38:59,230 --> 00:39:01,090
Will you pay for it if you break it?

393
00:39:01,110 --> 00:39:02,240
If you keep nagging,

394
00:39:02,550 --> 00:39:04,610
I'll throw you out with these things.

395
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:07,360
Let him go.

396
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:18,970
You scared me to death.

397
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:20,200
It was all your fault.

398
00:39:20,500 --> 00:39:21,510
You were supposed to take a picture of me.

399
00:39:21,510 --> 00:39:23,310
Why did you take a picture of her?

400
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:26,080
I'm prettier than her, aren't I?

401
00:39:27,590 --> 00:39:28,670
I find you

402
00:39:28,840 --> 00:39:30,300
have pretty bad eyesight.

403
00:39:36,630 --> 00:39:37,830
What did they ask you?

404
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:40,870
My identity, your identity,

405
00:39:40,870 --> 00:39:41,930
our relationship,

406
00:39:42,110 --> 00:39:43,840
and why we're going to Shanghai.

407
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:44,900
How did you answer?

408
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,530
Of course I said we're a couple.

409
00:39:48,150 --> 00:39:49,150
Should I have said

410
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:53,280
we escaped
from Chunguang Photo Studio together?

411
00:39:54,210 --> 00:39:56,410
Those people don't look like good guys.

412
00:39:59,190 --> 00:40:00,070
In these times,

413
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:03,840
staying alive is the most important thing.

414
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:10,800
Let me ask you.

415
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:14,700
Who is prettier, me or that woman?

416
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:20,330
True beauty lies in one's demeanor,
not appearance.

417
00:40:21,630 --> 00:40:22,960
What do you mean?

418
00:40:27,630 --> 00:40:29,840
I can be very elegant too, okay?

419
00:40:31,510 --> 00:40:33,710
Someday,
I'll show you how elegant I can be.

420
00:40:33,710 --> 00:40:34,910
It'll blow your mind.

421
00:40:36,510 --> 00:40:37,950
You'd better show it to those

422
00:40:37,950 --> 00:40:39,480
rich kids in the dance hall.

423
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,660
Something happened to my master.

424
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,660
I could be implicated at any time.

425
00:40:54,030 --> 00:40:56,230
Are you sure you still want to follow me?

426
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:02,590
In these times,

427
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:06,230
who else can I trust?

428
00:41:13,030 --> 00:41:15,490
We've lived in the same building
for so long.

429
00:41:15,950 --> 00:41:17,800
You usually ignore me.

430
00:41:18,980 --> 00:41:21,180
Do you look down on me for being a dancer?

431
00:41:21,230 --> 00:41:21,800
No.

432
00:41:24,840 --> 00:41:25,960
I really don't.

433
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:27,890
In these times,

434
00:41:28,310 --> 00:41:29,710
it's not easy for anyone.

435
00:41:30,450 --> 00:41:31,710
Then I should warn you,

436
00:41:32,470 --> 00:41:34,730
it's even harder to survive in Shanghai.

437
00:41:35,480 --> 00:41:37,480
Fortunately, I know a lot of people.

438
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,100
If you stick with me,

439
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:40,630
you'll have an easier time.

440
00:41:45,110 --> 00:41:46,640
What's your real last name?

441
00:41:47,170 --> 00:41:47,860
Chen.

442
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,890
Chen Kailai is my real name.

443
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:53,610
My grandmother said

444
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:57,060
I make the most money
with people surnamed Chen.

445
00:41:57,060 --> 00:41:58,390
When we get to Shanghai,

446
00:41:58,440 --> 00:41:59,500
just stick with me.

447
00:41:59,710 --> 00:42:01,000
Stop bragging.

448
00:42:02,030 --> 00:42:04,510
You called yourself Wang Xiaoni
when you rented the room.

449
00:42:04,510 --> 00:42:06,360
Some of the young masters
at the dance hall called you Xiaohui,

450
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,400
and some called you Meizhen.

451
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,920
You have so many names.

452
00:42:09,180 --> 00:42:12,440
Did your grandmother say
you could make money with anyone?

453
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,330
You have such a good memory.

454
00:42:14,740 --> 00:42:16,220
You remember all my names.

455
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:23,190
From now on,

456
00:42:24,330 --> 00:42:25,330
my name is Jinbao.

457
00:42:29,670 --> 00:42:31,030
My real name is Jinbao.

458
00:42:31,670 --> 00:42:33,550
That name sounds quite rich.

459
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:36,810
I have a younger sister.

460
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:38,340
Her name is Yinbao.

461
00:42:39,670 --> 00:42:41,530
If anything happens to me one day,

462
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:45,160
you must help me take care of her.

463
00:42:48,510 --> 00:42:50,230
We're not that close, are we?

464
00:42:57,840 --> 00:42:58,840
You're a good person.
